# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout.spl 69%
#
# Branch coverage, MEASURED (not estimated) on 2026-08-19 by running the
# Simple extractor for ALL NINE components (seven interactive/static widgets
# plus the css_zoo and dom_zoo coverage fixtures) under the deployed seed with
# SIMPLE_COVERAGE=1 / SIMPLE_COVERAGE_OUTPUT, unioning DecisionProbe rows by
# decision id across runs, and counting each decision's true/false branches:
#
#   simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout.spl        332/478 = 69%   (was 300/432)
#   simple_web_html_layout_renderer_core.spl          413/610 = 68%   (was 406/602)
#   simple_web_html_layout_renderer_foundation.spl    295/362 = 81%
#   simple_web_html_layout_renderer_decl_apply.spl    357/586 = 61%   (was 60%)
#   simple_web_html_layout_renderer_declarations.spl  165/254 = 65%   (was 64%)
#   simple_web_html_layout_renderer_style.spl          40/60  = 67%
#   dom_accessors.spl                                  93/146 = 64%
#   dom_identity_index.spl                             47/66  = 71%
#   dom.spl                                             8/14  = 57%
#   dom_api.spl                                         6/8   = 75%
#   script/script_host.spl                             16/20  = 80%
#   html_tree_builder.spl                             140/196 = 71%   (was 137/194)
#   html_tokenizer.spl                                166/242 = 69%
#   simple_web_css_property_id.spl                     45/72  = 62%
#   simple_web_css_box_effects.spl                     13/26  = 50%
#   layout_m14_types.spl                                7/8   = 88%
#   layout_table.spl                                    14/18 = 78%
#   paint_primitives.spl                                1/2   = 50%
#   ALL exercised browser_engine modules            2158/3168 = 68.1%   (was 2109/3104 = 67.9%)
#
# The >=80% goal is NOT met; the number is reported honestly. Re-measured
# 2026-08-19 after landing implicit-tbody synthesis and ::marker boxes (both
# bugs FIXED): the denominator grew again (3104 -> 3168 branch sides) because
# the new marker/tbody code paths add decisions, and coverage still rose
# 67.9% -> 68.1%. The residue is dominated by CSS properties/value forms no
# static fixture sets (decl_apply/declarations/core) and layout paths needing
# interaction. Closing to 80% needs more value-form fixtures, not a
# different oracle.
"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: button: click through the real event path relabels and re-layouts like Chrome
Audience: compiler and tooling engineers who maintain this spec

# Chrome <-> Simple Component-Set IO Differential

**Category:** Testing
**Status:** In Progress

## Purpose and Audience

Scales the phase-4 per-component harness from one counter widget to a
component SET: button, text_input, checkbox, list (reflow), table, and
float_text (float + line wrap). Each fixture is loaded by Chrome and by
Simple's browser_engine; interactive components drive their IO through each
engine's REAL event path; geometry is compared per state as canonical text.
Audience: anyone changing browser_engine layout, dispatch, or DOM mutation.

## Scope and Preconditions

Requires Chrome/Chromium and node. Driver (all components):
`sh tools/component_diff/run_component_diff.shs`. This spec gates on the
per-component retained evidence `tools/component_diff/out/<name>/summary.txt`,
fail-closed: missing/stale evidence or a fake chrome FAILS. The counter
component keeps its own spec (`chrome_counter_component_spec.spl`).

## Primary Workflow

1. Run the driver; read each component's `out/<name>/summary.txt`.
2. Assert non-vacuity (expected state count, >0 node lines compared).
3. Interactive components: assert the dispatch evidence and display-text
   agreement with Chrome's real JS; assert geometry changed / roundtrip.
4. Pin each component's measured divergence fail-closed (shrink-only).

## Key Concepts

| Concept | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Component set | 7 fixtures; interactions declared in fixture metas, mirrored per component in simple_component_dump.spl |
| Pixel divergence classes | body margin/height resolution, button text centering, text line height 17 vs 20 — same classes as counter |
| REAL defects pinned | table: FIXED 2026-08-19 (cells now columned; residual 14 = text metrics + body margin-collapse); float_text: FIXED 2026-08-19 (line boxes wrap beside the float; residual 6 = text metrics + body margin-collapse) — see bug records |

## Related Specifications

- [Component IO differential contract](../../../tools/component_diff/CONTRACT.md)
- [Counter component](chrome_counter_component_spec.spl)

## Evidence and Provenance

Measured against Google Chrome for Testing 151.0.7922.34, viewport 800x600,
2026-08-19. Bug records:
`doc/08_tracking/bug/browser_engine_table_layout_cells_stacked_vertically_2026-08-19.md`,
`doc/08_tracking/bug/browser_engine_float_no_inline_wrap_beside_float_2026-08-19.md`.

## Recovery and Troubleshooting

`UNAVAILABLE: no chrome executable found` — pass `--chrome` or set
`COMPONENT_DIFF_CHROME`. Stale evidence — re-run the driver.

## Compatibility and Limitations

Simple does not execute inline JS; each fixture's handler is mirrored by the
extractor AFTER the real typed-route dispatch (stated gap, CONTRACT.md).
The production applier has no append-child action, so the list component
adds/removes its item via a class-toggled `display:none` (still a real
reflow). Hover is deliberately not driven (no hover pipeline on this route).
"""

# @req: REQ-BROWSER_ENGI-ChroCompSet-001

use std.spec.*
use std.io_runtime.{shell_output, file_exists}

val TOOL_DIR: text = "tools/component_diff"

fn summary_path(component: text) -> text:
    TOOL_DIR + "/out/" + component + "/summary.txt"

fn summary_value(component: text, key: text) -> text:
    shell_output(
        "sed -n 's/^" + key + "=//p' " + summary_path(component) +
        " | head -1 | tr -d '\\n'"
    )

fn summary_i64(component: text, key: text) -> i64:
    val raw = summary_value(component, key)
    if raw == "":
        return -1
    raw.to_i64()

fn evidence_is_stale(component: text) -> bool:
    if not file_exists(summary_path(component)):
        return true
    val newer = shell_output(
        "find " + TOOL_DIR + "/fixtures/" + component + ".html " +
        TOOL_DIR + "/simple_component_dump.spl " +
        TOOL_DIR + "/chrome_component_dump.js " +
        TOOL_DIR + "/component_geom_diff.spl " +
        TOOL_DIR + "/run_component_diff.shs " +
        "-newer " + summary_path(component) +
        " 2>/dev/null | head -1 | tr -d '\\n'"
    )
    newer != ""

# Shared fail-closed gate: fresh evidence, real chrome, expected states,
# nonzero node lines, divergence pinned at the measured baseline.
fn assert_component(component: text, states: i64, nodes: i64, pin_per_state: [i64]):
    step("Evidence for " + component + " must exist and be fresh")
    expect(evidence_is_stale(component)).to_equal(false)  # oracle: missing/stale FAILS; run sh tools/component_diff/run_component_diff.shs
    step("A real Chrome must have produced the chrome side")
    expect(summary_value(component, "chrome_version").contains("Chrome/")).to_equal(true)
    step("All states compared over a nonzero node-line count")
    expect(summary_i64(component, "states_compared")).to_equal(states)
    expect(summary_i64(component, "nodes_compared")).to_equal(nodes)  # oracle: pin cannot be gamed by dropping nodes
    step("Measured divergence baseline per state: shrink-only ratchet")
    expect(summary_i64(component, "divergent_total") >= 0).to_equal(true)  # oracle: missing summary reads -1, FAILS
    var k: i64 = 0
    var total: i64 = 0
    while k < states:
        expect(summary_i64(component, "divergent_s" + k.to_string()) <= pin_per_state[k]).to_equal(true)
        total = total + pin_per_state[k]
        k = k + 1
    expect(summary_i64(component, "divergent_total") <= total).to_equal(true)

fn assert_io_roundtrip(component: text):
    step("Interaction must CHANGE geometry in BOTH engines, then return EXACTLY to the initial state")
    expect(summary_i64(component, "geometry_changed_chrome")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
    expect(summary_i64(component, "geometry_changed_simple")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
    expect(summary_i64(component, "roundtrip_chrome")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
    expect(summary_i64(component, "roundtrip_simple")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract

describe "Chrome to Simple component-set IO differential":
    it "button: click through the real event path relabels and re-layouts like Chrome":
        step("Verify: button: click through the real event path relabels and re-layouts like Chrome")
        # @req: REQ-BROWSER_ENGI-ChroCompSet-001
        assert_component("button", 2, 7, [6, 6])
        step("Dispatch collected the fixture's REAL inline onclick and the button default action")
        expect(summary_i64("button", "dispatch_btn_actions")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_value("button", "dispatch_btn_inline_onclick")).to_equal("yes")
        expect(summary_value("button", "dispatch_btn_default")).to_equal("button-activate")
        step("Click must change geometry in both engines; label text must agree at both states")
        expect(summary_i64("button", "geometry_changed_chrome")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_i64("button", "geometry_changed_simple")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_value("button", "display_s0_chrome")).to_equal("default")
        expect(summary_value("button", "display_s1_chrome")).to_equal("clicked")
        expect(summary_i64("button", "display_match")).to_equal(2)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_i64("button", "display_total")).to_equal(2)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract

    it "text_input: typing through the session input route echoes value and widens the caret area":
        step("Verify: text_input: typing through the session input route echoes value and widens the caret area")
        # @req: REQ-BROWSER_ENGI-ChroCompSet-001
        assert_component("text_input", 2, 7, [4, 4])
        step("The input-event dispatch collected the fixture's REAL inline oninput")
        expect(summary_i64("text_input", "dispatch_field_actions")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_value("text_input", "dispatch_field_inline_onclick")).to_equal("yes")
        step("Typing must change geometry (echo text + caret-area class) in both engines")
        expect(summary_i64("text_input", "geometry_changed_chrome")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_i64("text_input", "geometry_changed_simple")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        step("Echoed value agrees with Chrome's real JS at both states")
        expect(summary_value("text_input", "display_s0_chrome")).to_equal("empty")
        expect(summary_value("text_input", "display_s1_chrome")).to_equal("hello")
        expect(summary_i64("text_input", "display_match")).to_equal(2)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_i64("text_input", "display_total")).to_equal(2)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract

    it "checkbox: toggling exercises the input-checkbox-toggle default action and roundtrips":
        step("Verify: checkbox: toggling exercises the input-checkbox-toggle default action and roundtrips")
        # @req: REQ-BROWSER_ENGI-ChroCompSet-001
        assert_component("checkbox", 3, 6, [4, 4, 4])
        step("Both clicks must yield the checkbox toggle default action and the REAL inline flip()")
        expect(summary_i64("checkbox", "dispatch_cb_actions")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_value("checkbox", "dispatch_cb_inline_onclick")).to_equal("yes")
        expect(summary_value("checkbox", "dispatch_cb_default")).to_equal("input-checkbox-toggle")
        assert_io_roundtrip("checkbox")
        step("State text agrees with Chrome's real JS at every state")
        expect(summary_value("checkbox", "display_s0_chrome")).to_equal("off")
        expect(summary_value("checkbox", "display_s1_chrome")).to_equal("on")
        expect(summary_value("checkbox", "display_s2_chrome")).to_equal("off")
        expect(summary_i64("checkbox", "display_match")).to_equal(3)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_i64("checkbox", "display_total")).to_equal(3)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract

    it "list: adding and removing an item reflows following siblings and roundtrips":
        step("Verify: list: adding and removing an item reflows following siblings and roundtrips")
        # @req: REQ-BROWSER_ENGI-ChroCompSet-001
        assert_component("list", 3, 14, [20, 22, 20])
        step("Both button dispatches collected the REAL inline show() and the button default action")
        expect(summary_i64("list", "dispatch_add_actions")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_value("list", "dispatch_add_inline_onclick")).to_equal("yes")
        expect(summary_i64("list", "dispatch_rm_actions")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
        expect(summary_value("list", "dispatch_rm_default")).to_equal("button-activate")
        assert_io_roundtrip("list")

    it "table: static 2x3 table layout is compared and its REAL divergence is pinned":
        step("Verify: table: static 2x3 table layout is compared and its REAL divergence is pinned")
        # @req: REQ-BROWSER_ENGI-ChroCompSet-001
        # Simple stacks cells vertically — a REAL defect, filed:
        # doc/08_tracking/bug/browser_engine_table_layout_cells_stacked_vertically_2026-08-19.md
        # FIXED 2026-08-19: table/tbody/rows/cells match Chrome exactly (36 -> 14).
        # Residual 14 lines: 6 text-node pairs (font advance/line-height metrics)
        # + body (margin-collapse through the table's margin). Shrink-only pin.
        assert_component("table", 1, 18, [14])

    it "float_text: float plus wrapping text is compared and its REAL divergence is pinned":
        step("Verify: float_text: float plus wrapping text is compared and its REAL divergence is pinned")
        # @req: REQ-BROWSER_ENGI-ChroCompSet-001
        # doc/08_tracking/bug/browser_engine_float_no_inline_wrap_beside_float_2026-08-19.md
        # FIXED 2026-08-19: float:left registers an exclusion band; the
        # paragraph's line boxes wrap narrowed beside the float and resume
        # full width past its margin-box bottom (14 -> 6). #para, #wrap,
        # #after and html match Chrome exactly. Residual 6 lines: 2 text-node
        # pairs (font advance/line-height metrics) + body (margin-collapse).
        # Shrink-only pin.
        assert_component("float_text", 1, 8, [6])

    it "css_zoo: static property-zoo page is compared and its divergence is pinned":
        step("Verify: css_zoo: static property-zoo page is compared and its divergence is pinned")
        # @req: REQ-BROWSER_ENGI-ChroCompSet-001
        # Coverage fixture: exercises shorthand arities (margin/padding 1-4),
        # per-side borders, font/text/display/position/overflow/min-max/%/em/
        # rem/background/opacity/z-index/visibility/box-sizing branches plus
        # invalid-value rejection branches (bad1..bad5). All 148 divergent
        # lines are the known text-metrics class (17px vs 20px text heights
        # and the 1px cumulative y drift they cause) — no structural defect;
        # every element box path matches Chrome. Shrink-only pin.
        assert_component("css_zoo", 1, 140, [148])

    it "dom_zoo: static tree-builder-zoo page is compared and its REAL divergences are pinned":
        step("Verify: dom_zoo: static tree-builder-zoo page is compared and its REAL divergences are pinned")
        # @req: REQ-BROWSER_ENGI-ChroCompSet-001
        # Coverage fixture: comments, entities, implicit p/li closure,
        # quoted/unquoted attrs, void elements, deep nesting, pre/whitespace.
        # TWO REAL structural defects were found, filed, and FIXED 2026-08-19:
        # doc/08_tracking/bug/browser_engine_no_implicit_tbody_synthesis_2026-08-19.md
        #   (implicit <tbody> now synthesized for tr/td/th directly in <table>)
        # doc/08_tracking/bug/browser_engine_no_list_marker_boxes_2026-08-19.md
        #   (::marker boxes now generated per <li>)
        # Node-path sets are now IDENTICAL to Chrome (comm -3 on state0 paths
        # = 0 lines; was 5 chrome-only ::marker + tbody-shape mismatch).
        # Node count rose 64 -> 70 because the synthesized tbody + 5 markers
        # are now compared; divergent lines 139 -> 145 for the same reason —
        # every residual line is the known text-metrics class (marker/text
        # heights 18 vs 16/17 and small y drift), no structural defect.
        # Shrink-only pin on the divergence; structural parity is the win.
        assert_component("dom_zoo", 1, 70, [145])
